From: Horizon authors <>
Subject: [PATCH] Place Continue at the completed pan endpoint before input

The former queued pan used an absolute target after the first field view was
set. Removing it exposed the additive load adjustments and a stale GTE view
left by model/collision initialization. In Green Gym the tamer is clipped.

Share the existing clamped endpoint calculation with a synchronous Continue
initializer. Restore the field view/projection and place the camera at that
endpoint after saved positions/collision relocation. The existing tile upload
then covers the final view before field input. Script pans retain their state
machine, rounding, streaming and large-partner shift. No pan object or new
resident state is added to Continue.

diff --git a/include/dw/map.h b/include/dw/map.h
index 75a671c2..c602b1a3 100644
--- a/include/dw/map.h
+++ b/include/dw/map.h
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ extern int8_t MAP_TILE_Y;
 extern MapLightUpdateData MAP_LIGHT_UPDATE_DATA[];
 
 void initializeDrawingOffsets(MapTileData *tiles);
+void initializeLoadedDrawingOffsets(void);
 void clearMapObjects(LocalMapObjectInstance *instances);
 void calcMapObjectOrder(LocalMapObjectInstance *instances);
 void renderMapOverlays(LocalMapObjectInstance *instances, int16_t screenX, int16_t screenY);
diff --git a/src/main/main.c b/src/main/main.c
index 3534bbda..784f88c6 100644
--- a/src/main/main.c
+++ b/src/main/main.c
@@ -3984,7 +3984,7 @@ void initializeLoadedMap(void)
 	 * A second, queued pan keeps aiming at this snapshot while the tamer
